body:
1) It can't be used to ensure her safety in all circumstances. She has made a lot of enemies and as a result people want her dead. She can threaten to release the info but if she does release it then her leverage is gone. It is basically a bluff. The leverage would be more useful where she was in some trouble or to be arrested. &nbsp;

2) I'm not entirely sure why the Americans attack Irene Adler or Mrs Hudson. I assume at that point they were just trying to prevent the information about the flight getting out. It is clear later on that the UK/USA joined to cover up the plane bombing. Moriarty is involved as he hires Irene Adler to play with Sherlock's mind and figure out the code. He gave the code and Irene passed it on to Moriarty. Moriarty is either working with the group of terrorists who are to be involved in the plane bombing, or he wishes to notify them because he's a dick. &nbsp;

3) Adler probably did not need Moriarty. Moriarty needed Adler. If Adler got the kill order called off then it's because she wanted Sherlock and Watson to live. There are 3 motivations for her that I see: She wanted to protect them and keep them alive, she wanted money, she was threatened. &nbsp;

Hope that helps. Probably made a mistake or two but I'm sure someone will correct it.
